<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Luc-en-Diois</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Luc-en-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diois">Diois</a> is a village in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/drome">Drôme</a> valley in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, the site of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucus-augusti">Lucus Augusti</a>, one of the two chief towns of the Celtic Vocontii under Roman rule, alongside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaison-la-romaine">Vasio</a> (Vaison-la-Romaine). Its role as a centre was later taken over by nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/die-drome">Dea Augusta</a>, modern Die. The territory of the Vocontii formed part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gallia-narbonensis">Gallia Narbonensis</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luc-en-diois.jpg" alt="Luc-en-Diois" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MOSSOT · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Luc-en-Diois_-_Mairie.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
